<section id="optimal-paths" class="process-section optimal-section">
  <div class="container process-shell-wide">
    <div class="process-heading">
      <span class="section-kicker">Optimal path computation</span>
      <h2>Optimal trust path computation.</h2>
      <p>
        Once admissible trust relationships are represented as a governed weighted
        graph, certification path selection becomes a shortest-path problem over valid
        candidates. PolarisChain optimizes path choice instead of accepting the first
        route returned by heuristic traversal.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="optimal-layout">
      <article class="optimal-formula-card">
        <span class="optimal-label">Objective function</span>
        <div class="optimal-equation-wrap">
          <p class="optimal-equation" aria-label="P star equals arg min over P in Paths of the sum over e in P of w of e">
            <span class="math-var-light">P</span>* = <span class="math-var-light">argmin</span><sub><span class="math-var-light">P</span> &isin; <span class="math-var-light">Paths</span></sub>
            <span class="math-sum">&Sigma;</span><sub><span class="math-var-light">e</span> &isin; <span class="math-var-light">P</span></sub>
            <span class="math-var-light">w</span>(<span class="math-var-light">e</span>)
          </p>
        </div>
        <p>
          Among all valid certification paths, the chosen route is the one with the
          minimum accumulated edge cost under the defined trust model.
        </p>
      </article>

      <div class="optimal-grid">
        <article class="optimal-card">
          <h3>Deterministic optimization</h3>
          <p>
            Dijkstra-based computation is applied over the governed weighted graph so
            the selected trust path is the mathematically optimal route under the cost
            model, not a heuristic guess.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="optimal-card">
          <h3>Multi-criteria scoring</h3>
          <p>
            Edge weights can combine cryptographic profile, algorithm family, key
            strength, policy compatibility, and structural distance into a single
            comparable score.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="optimal-card">
          <h3>Explainable trust paths</h3>
          <p>
            Because each path is evaluated through explicit edge costs, the selected
            chain can be justified in terms of governance, cryptographic quality, and
            structural efficiency.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

